issue_context.body:
**Context:**
- Playwright Version: 1.16.3
- Operating System: Mac
- Node.js version: 17.0.1
- Browser: Chromium

<!-- CLI to auto-capture this info -->
<!-- npx envinfo --preset playwright --markdown -->

**Code Snippet**

```typescript
import { test } from "@playwright/test";

test("example", async ({ page }) => {
	await page.goto("https://www.google.com");
	const s = page.locator("input[name=q]");
	await s.fill("example");
	await page.waitForTimeout(5000);
	await s.fill("overwritten");
	await page.waitForTimeout(5000);
});

```

**Describe the bug**

When trying to select other times (rewind/forward) on the video, the clip continues to play from its current location.

When I play the video in `test-results`, I can rewind/forward it as expected

